[{"sha":"d3c846f8b0279e79b0e3a960a7575fde6920e9df","node_id":"C_kwDOJ0Z1PtoAKGQzYzg0NmY4YjAyNzllNzliMGUzYTk2MGE3NTc1ZmRlNjkyMGU5ZGY","commit":{"author":{"name":"Gigrise","email":"34164295+Gigrise@users.noreply.github.com","date":"2026-10-07T04:39:34Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-10-07T04:39:34Z"},"message":"llama: fix clef head reads past 2GiB on windows (#18777)\n\nThe Clef head read its weights with std::ifstream::seekg. The Windows\nllama-server ships with libc++ 18.1.8, where that seek truncates the\noffset to 32 bits. clef-flash stores the clef.* tensors at about 9.5GB,\nso the head loaded backbone bytes as its weights and every\n/v1/systemone request failed with \"Clef: non-finite logit\". clef:27b\nkeeps the head and output.weight below 2GB and was unaffected.\n\nRead with ggml_fopen and an explicit 64-bit seek instead, as read_at\nin llama/compat already does.\n\nFixes #18769","tree":{"sha":"48621aa6bc3c622806056143ef781a093944c841","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ollama/ollama/git/trees/48621aa6bc3c622806056143ef781a093944c841"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ollama/ollama/git/commits/d3c846f8b0279e79b0e3a960a7575fde6920e9df","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqxc0GCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA7AgQAFI/GcChNLwEfbZnKJSIdgiA\nY08XJI3NqBVXRQtt3t5kj4ySaK+rA0hNYaMoxakTQ+eRx3ttWaLlGxzYaEj6g9hX\nsnxx4tqeK8++brpGZ117BB/kWSqW2Qd+a+RadU4fpiBY26b4PBoVcc5EuHXchR7s\ngbCyOUNwD3ETHSAKCVfrBK5lEWwEiKkOJLeexRDtYlRe4wkhzHDlIijuR8KdZwxc\nCmAeDeQ67tnfynkd8t0mF7ssGI5BnRmJwTsKTrG8ZaVg4nEwMFFi5JeFJOLYH5j2\nDMhp/zJm2B6yQczG9WnxagNuAKjbwutctx6GoINAm6IX+bOVTttG2ox7c5ojJjo3\nX/JgQitn0/HwmXOtbuwjWjX13WYvqJtMk8JNIVAt1pvakjtn4xpBzcJWFovW9brS\nJS0ue0vXBiXZzRBQZgexZX1fhznNYjgc90Wu+1DppVXRdv+jbFKb6raxIwTC4Rak\nzXiy2UST1+Pe80z5CBDfQL4YkuWA8BdDF3tDK0k4ggaaMFLEOAXoN97goturEVuT\n4jB9rrpcisYSwCb9EaqkXFroYz2hhXELiZJKOOjAVXSjLIgnlNmUCH3d4ltB7D9u\nwURXflmQPt7sdG+LQc/hiWnhjCkHJTYcPdBIBb6E/3vJ2TNhSrxQVxmVNQqX/6B6\n/oK085/FnCn81irpNGHh\n=ST/4\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 48621aa6bc3c622806056143ef781a093944c841\nparent f864601538bd283dbcd011244db99e2760b125c1\nauthor Gigrise <34164295+Gigrise@users.noreply.github.com> 1791347974 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791347974 -0700\n\nllama: fix clef head reads past 2GiB on windows (#18777)\n\nThe Clef head read its weights with std::ifstream::seekg. The Windows\nllama-server ships with libc++ 18.1.8, where that seek truncates the\noffset to 32 bits. clef-flash stores the clef.* tensors at about 9.5GB,\nso the head loaded backbone bytes as its weights and every\n/v1/systemone request failed with \"Clef: non-finite logit\". clef:27b\nkeeps the head and output.weight below 2GB and was unaffected.\n\nRead with ggml_fopen and an explicit 64-bit seek instead, as read_at\nin llama/compat already does.\n\nFixes #18769","verified_at":"2026-10-07T04:39:35Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ollama/ollama/commits/d3c846f8b0279e79b0e3a960a7575fde6920e9df","html_url":"https://github.com/ollama/ollama/commit/d3c846f8b0279e79b0e3a960a7575fde6920e9df","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ollama/ollama/commits/d3c846f8b0279e79b0e3a960a7575fde6920e9df/comments","author":{"login":"Gigrise","id":34164295,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM0MTY0Mjk1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/34164295?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Gigrise","html_url":"https://github.com/Gigrise","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Gigrise/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Gigrise/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Gigrise/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Gigrise/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Gigrise/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Gigrise/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Gig